## Relationships

### Semantic
- [CXC-BPO] RELATED_TO [CXC-HKR] — peer delivery endpoints on the one decision-ops surface, deliberately NOT merged
- [CXC-BPO-MCP] DEPENDS_ON [CXC-BPO-DERIVE-NOT-AUTHOR] — the endpoint's whole receipt is meaningless if the rows are authored
- [CXC-BPO-STALE-GATE] PART_OF [CXC-BPO-PROVENANCE-GATE] — the staleness check is the provenance block's second use
- [CXC-BPO-NEGATIVE-CONTROL] PART_OF [CXC-BPO-DERIVE-NOT-AUTHOR] — the injectors are what make "derived" a falsifiable claim
- [CXC-BPO-THREE-STATES] DEPENDS_ON [CXC-BPO-DERIVE-NOT-AUTHOR] — BLOCKED and UNVERIFIED are only meaningful about a derived sheet
- [CXC-BPO-SEAM] RELATED_TO [CXC-HKR-MCP] — the endpoint this one is deliberately not a mode of
- [CXC-BPO-SEAM] RELATED_TO [CXC-HKR-FAULT-INJECTOR] — the same keep-the-injector-public discipline, one surface over
- [CXC-BPO-MCP] DEPENDS_ON [CXC-BPO-LAUNCHER] — the endpoint's publish leg is only legitimate BECAUSE a consumer exists; without it the publish is the into-the-void defect the scope-boundary refused
- [CXC-BPO-LAUNCHER] RELATED_TO [CXC-HKR-LAUNCHER] — the sibling consumer, same lands-with-the-endpoint rule, different viewer choice
- [CXC-BPO-LAUNCHER] DEPENDS_ON [CXC-MDV] — the window IS the read-only markdown doc viewer, reused by reference and not forked
